= Scope and standing
A search round over records (AGENTS.md "Research searches must leave visual reports"). It re-reads every prime-field $E(bb(F)_p)$ index-calculus lead the lab has written down, in three layers: the 30 `ic-prime` atlas leads plus 63 prime-relevant atlas leads of other families (read through the decrypted 2026-11-07 survey and the 2026-11-10 sweep, since the atlas itself is vault-encrypted and `KEY` is unavailable here); the 183 idea-campaign records of crypto-autoresearcher PRs \#3183–\#3260 (plaintext PR heads, extracted today); and 68 post-atlas proposals recorded in this repository (closure ledger, five-lab chase, P/S proposals, equation-budget note, sub-exponential probes, Iwasawa and moonshot records, encyclopedia cells 0.1/0.2/A12). 304 records; 237 in scope; 67 out of scope (binary, Koblitz, $bb(F)_(p^k)$ covers, Curve25519 formula audits, quantum).

No pcc claim, no `bench.record/v1`, no isolab run, no leaderboard or benchmark row, no atlas edit. research-kb and ecdb were unavailable (gap recorded); novelty rests on grep.

= Method
Nine Sonnet workers (one assignment each), a Haiku validator (schema, enums, duplicate ids, 1,298 cited paths resolved, 0 missing) and an Opus red team over every open, blocked and flagship record plus 12 sampled desk-only refutations. Each lead gets one verdict (refuted, engineering, open, blocked, unexamined, out-of-scope), one evidence strength (proof, measured, toy, desk, none), one mechanism column, the newest sources, and the cheapest next test. Workers ran the record's own cheapest check when it was stdlib Python under three CPU-minutes: 71 such checks today, all in the scratchpad, none replayed.

